          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Klein-Gordon equation
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+differential+equation"} linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+differential+equation"} partial differential equation
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation+of+motion"} equation of motion
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            of possibly non-vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            on some (possibly
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curved+spacetime"} curved
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifold"}> Lorentzian manifold
            ): it is the relativistic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+equation"} wave equation
            with inhomogeneity the mass
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi m
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m^2
          %p
            The structure of the Klein-Gordon equation appears also in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of richer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            than just
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+fields"} scalar fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            may more generally be some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+solutions"} fundamental solutions
            of the Klein-Gordon equation, called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagators"} propagators
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FundamentalSolutions"} below
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            (a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo-Riemannian manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \in \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
            %em Klein-Gordon equation
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equation
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
