          %h3#bicharacteristic_flow_and_propagation_of_singularities Bicharacteristic flow and propagation of singularities
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicharacteristic+strips"} bicharacteristic strips
            of the Klein-Gordon operator are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+vectors"} cotangent vectors
            along
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lightlike"} lightlike
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesics"} geodesics
            (
            %a{:href => "bicharacteristic+flow#BicharachteristicFlowOfKleinGordonOperator"}> this example
            ).
          %h3#FundamentalSolutions Fundamental solutions
          %p
            On a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetime"} globally hyperbolic spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            the Klein-Gordon equation has unique advanced and retarded
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+functions"} Green functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi R
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ×
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_R \in \mathcal{D}'(M\times M)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ×
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_A \in \mathcal{D}'(M\times M)
            respectively.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+and+retarded+Green+functions"} advanced and retarded Green functions
            are uniquely distinguished by their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support+of+a+distribution"} support
            properties. Namely,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} supp
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y) \in \operatorname{supp} \Delta_R
            only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+future"} causal future
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} supp
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y) \in \operatorname{supp} \Delta_A
            only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+past"} causal past
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
          %p
            Their difference
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi R
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_S = \Delta_R - \Delta_A
            is a bisolution known as the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peierls+bracket"} Peierls bracket
            which gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
            of the free scalar field, which yields the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of the free scalar field to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
          %p
            Other important Green functions or bisolutions include any (anti-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{\bar{F}}
            )
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_F
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+propagator"} Hadamard propagator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(x,y)
            in a geodesically convex neighborhood of the diagonal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x=y
            to be of a special
            = succeed "." do
