            %p
              (see also
              = succeed "\u2018s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikica+Kocic"} Kocic
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/KGPropagatorsOnMinkowskiTable.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            These propagators govern the construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+observables"} quantum observables
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
            on the given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetime"} globally hyperbolic spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interacting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory+on+curved+spacetimes"} on curved spacetimes
            via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+covariant+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} locally covariant perturbative quantum field theory
            for more on this.
          %h3#relation_to_schrdinger_equation Relation to Schrödinger equation
          %p
            Sometimes the Klein-Gordon equation is thought of as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"} relativistic
            refinement of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schr%C3%B6dinger+equation"} Schrödinger equation
            (as one passes from the non-relativistic to the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+particle"} relativistic particle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+function"} wave function
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+equation"}> wave equation
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave"} wave
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane+wave"} plane wave
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+vector"}> wave vector
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavelength"} wavelength
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frequency"} frequency
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+analysis"} Fourier analysis
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heat+equation"} heat equation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+equation"} wave equation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schr%C3%B6dinger+equation"} Schrödinger equation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+equation"} Dirac equation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sine-Gordon+equation"} sine-Gordon equation
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The Klein-Gordon equation is named after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oskar+Klein"} Oskar Klein
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Gordon"} Walter Gordon
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+D.+Bjorken"}> James D. Bjorken
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sidney+D.+Drell"} Sidney D. Drell
              = succeed "," do
                %em Relativistic Quantum Mechanics
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://archive.org/details/relativisticquan0000bjor/page/n1/mode/2up"} ark:/13960/t5fc2v05h
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://emineter.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/james-d-bjorken-sidney-d-drell-relativistic-quantum-mechanics-1964.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mmmut.ac.in/News_content/14331tpnews_11122020.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            An overview over the KG
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagators"} propagators
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            is given in
          %ul
            %li#Kocic16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikica+Kocic"}> Mikica Kocic
              ,
              %em Invariant Commutation and Propagation Functions Invariant Commutation and Propagation Functions
              (2016) &amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/KGPropagatorsOnMinkowskiTable.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+propagator"} Hadamard propagator
            for the Klein-Gordon equation on general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetimes"} globally hyperbolic spacetimes
            was found in
          %ul
            %li#Radzikowski96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marek+Radzikowski"}> Marek Radzikowski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Micro-local approach to the Hadamard condition in quantum field theory on curved space-time
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104287114"} Euclid
          %p The original reference on the relevant notions of microlocal analysis and distinguished parametrices of the Klein-Gordon equation is
          %ul
            %li#DuistermaatHoermander72
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johann+Duistermaat"}> Johann Duistermaat
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lars+H%C3%B6rmander"} Lars Hörmander
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fourier integral operators. II
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/bf02392165"} doi
          %p Textbook accounts include
          %ul
            %li#BaerGinouxPfaeffle07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+B%C3%A4r"}> Christian Bär
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Ginoux"} Nicolas Ginoux
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Pf%C3%A4ffle"} Frank Pfäffle
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wave Equations on Lorentzian Manifolds and Quantization
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.1036"} arXiv:0806.1036
            %li#Ginoux08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Ginoux"}> Nicolas Ginoux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Linear wave equations
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+B%C3%A4r"} Christian Bär
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Field Theory on Curved Spacetimes: Concepts and Methods
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Klein%E2%80%93Gordon_equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
